WEBVTT

00:00:02.020 --> 00:00:03.510
Rokei-Rokei-Rokei.

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:04.910
Takei-Takei-Takei.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.400
Rokei-Rokei-Rokei.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:07.400
Takei-Takei-Takei.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:08.850
Rokei-Rokei-Rokei.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:11.800
Okay, that's all the training for today!

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.110
Thank you very much!

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:14.980
Good morning.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:18.640
You've both got school this morning, 
and you're training?

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.560
Yes!

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.290
Don't know how you do it this early.

00:00:22.290 --> 00:00:23.170
It's natural!

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.290
Being a mage is about putting 
in daily practice.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.400
Doing something daily, even if 
only a little, is important.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:33.550
I keep saying this, but I'm not 
trying to become a mage...

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:34.980
Why not?

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.720
You could be a high school mage.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.640
<b>The High School Mage 

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.630
<i>The High School Mage, Yushi</i>!

00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:45.560
One day, our hero, Yushi Inaba, 
finds a magic book,

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:49.310
and battles one monster 
after another at school!

00:00:49.310 --> 00:00:50.180
Let's go.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:54.430
Lend me your power, <i>Petit Hierozoicon</i>!

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.660
What kind of manga or light novel is that?

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.910
My high school is normal!

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:02.510
That's right.

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:06.010
And that's a really lazy backstory, Reimei.

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.120
Jeez, really...

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.930
That's a dream. It's impossible.

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.460
Good grief, chirp, right?

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:49.940
<b>Ninth Haunting 
New Term</b>

00:02:49.940 --> 00:02:51.200
Bye!

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.330
<i>As of today, I'm a second-year.</i>

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.770
<i>It's the first time I've been back at school 
since returning to the apartment.</i>

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:09.110
<i>Was I like that last year?</i>

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:14.290
Master, you're going to 
school now, aren't you?

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:15.700
That's right.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.200
Fool? Stay in my pocket!

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.940
I'm sorry.

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:27.040
Our job is to protect you, master.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.640
I shall always be with you.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:32.300
<i>I left this thing at home.</i>

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:34.530
I said "always"...

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:35.720
I know!

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:38.480
Be sure not to come out around others!

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:39.980
Of course.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:44.080
Mommy, he's talking to a doll.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.180
Don't look at him!

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.080
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:55.660
Jeez, what a way to start the day...

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:58.860
Hey! Good morning!

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:01.910
Tashiro!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.330
This year, we're in the same class!

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:05.710
Glad to be with you, Inaba.

00:04:05.710 --> 00:04:08.380
Same club and same class.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.080
Must be fate, huh?

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:11.080
That's right.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:14.660
The way you saved me, I really 
do feel like it's fate!

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:18.230
Jeez, you two. If you're going
to say that, you mean destiny.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.870
Whoops, I got it wrong!

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.500
Hey, Inaba, did you lose weight?

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:26.460
You seem more trim, somehow...

00:04:26.770 --> 00:04:28.080
D-Do I?

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.240
Jeez, Ta-ko, the way you're 
moving your hands is dirty.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:33.940
Oh?

00:04:33.110 --> 00:04:35.910
How closely are you looking at him?

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.840
<i>Girls are so...</i>

00:04:39.350 --> 00:04:41.570
Way to go, master.

00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:43.670
They all love you.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:46.600
No! And you stay in there!

00:04:51.170 --> 00:04:53.270
<i>And the new year began.</i>

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.700
And so, this relative pronoun goes here...

00:05:00.050 --> 00:05:01.520
And this is what happens.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:08.300
<i>I guess the only difference was that 
there was a new English teacher.</i>

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:10.650
<i>Katsumasa Miura.</i>

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.370
<i>He's probably still in his 20s.</i>

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.600
<i>He's only been a teacher 
for three or four years.</i>

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:20.720
<i>His teaching style is clear, and I guess 
he seems serious or smart, but...</i>

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.550
That's all for today.

00:05:29.060 --> 00:05:33.300
Sensei, there was a part in that 
last example I didn't get.

00:05:33.590 --> 00:05:37.500
Next class, I'll cover it in detail.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.040
R-Right...

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:43.290
<i>But he's a little hard to get to know.</i>

00:05:44.810 --> 00:05:49.060
I heard when Miura was in college, 
he did plays and stuff.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:50.630
Plays?

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:52.900
Underground stuff?

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:57.270
No. He got lead roles in 
Shakespeare plays and stuff.

00:05:57.270 --> 00:05:58.820
Surprising, huh?

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:01.750
<i>Where did she even learn that?</i>

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:05.970
But Shakespeare is really classic 
and straightforward, right?

00:06:05.970 --> 00:06:09.520
He doesn't seem like the kind of guy 
who'd do something so showy...

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:11.000
That's right.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.580
All his classes follow the book, 
without deviation.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.410
And they're totally boring.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:16.250
Right?

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.680
So I figured it out...

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:23.110
Something happened at his old school.

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:29.240
What? Oh, jeez...

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:36.440
<i>I don't know what could've happened.</i>

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:41.040
<i>But seeing how dark he looks, 
I can believe it.</i>

00:06:43.950 --> 00:06:45.080
<i>Miura!</i>

00:06:50.110 --> 00:06:51.690
<i>What's he doing?</i>

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.950
<i>Practice has started.</i>

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.940
<i>Is he watching them?</i>

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.410
What?

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:11.030
I felt really angry.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.360
Those eyes, like a dead fish... 
I've never noticed them before.

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.960
I could see myself punching him, someday.

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:20.870
No, no...

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:23.440
Miura isn't even my homeroom teacher,

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:25.280
and he has nothing to do with the club.

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.930
I'll just stay away from him.

00:07:31.910 --> 00:07:35.840
Master, who was that?

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.350
<i>And so, I went back to my daily life.</i>

00:07:41.350 --> 00:07:43.980
<b>Welcome New Members!</b>

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:45.700
<i>The spring of my second 
year passed peacefully.</i>

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.310
<i>And then, Golden Week came.</i>

00:07:50.830 --> 00:07:51.900
I'm so tired...

00:07:58.430 --> 00:08:00.210
Good work on your training!

00:08:00.210 --> 00:08:01.920
Want some cold water?

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:04.210
Stop slacking off!

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:06.570
Who cares if I do?

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:08.930
<i>On his days off,</i>

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:11.750
<i>Hase began spending all his 
time at the Yokai Apartments.</i>

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.920
I can't help it... This place is comfy.

00:08:15.160 --> 00:08:18.080
The food is good, and the bath feels great.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:19.540
And Kuri's here.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:21.180
Right, Kuri?

00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:24.810
He's feeling more and more like a dad.

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:26.770
There, there.

00:08:27.100 --> 00:08:29.460
And look at this yard...

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:32.190
The flowers are blooming out of season.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:35.000
It kind of purifies the heart—

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:40.600
That... isn't a flower.

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:45.290
Wow! It isn't a flower!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:47.040
That's the Yokai Apartments for you!

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.630
What's wrong?

00:08:56.630 --> 00:08:58.590
C-Could it be...

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:02.220
Ryu-san!

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:05.260
It's been a long time.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:07.200
No, I should say, "Welcome home."

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.310
Glad to have you back, Yushi-kun.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:10.980
Thanks!

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:14.770
Your aura's changed, Yushi-kun.

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:17.660
I heard that you befriended a magic book.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:20.680
Th-That's right! I'll go get it!

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.850
This is my best friend, Hase Mizuki!

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.160
Um... sorry.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.510
Not at all.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.130
This has some amazing stuff in it.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:46.920
You can tell?

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:49.240
I can get a mental image.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.330
Wow...

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:55.370
But I'm glad it isn't the real <i>Hierozoicon</i>.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.490
<i>That's same thing Akine-chan said.</i>

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:04.070
It was sudden, so I can see 
why you'd be surprised.

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:05.590
But it's nothing to worry about.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:09.180
Furuhonya-san said the same thing.

00:10:09.470 --> 00:10:13.410
But it feels like I can believe 
it more when you say it...

00:10:13.900 --> 00:10:15.210
Does it?

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:17.090
I mean, if you're both mages,

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:21.260
I'd rather have learned it from you!

00:10:24.300 --> 00:10:26.890
I'm sorry you don't like me!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.020
You think you're in a position to be picky?

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.660
Huh? Huh? Huh?

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.390
Sorry! Sorry!

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:37.820
Hey, welcome back.

00:10:37.820 --> 00:10:39.850
Hello, Furuhonya-san.

00:10:39.850 --> 00:10:41.450
How many years has it been?

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:44.370
Hey, is Ryu back?

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:48.580
<b>Maou</b>

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:47.530
We'll have a party tonight to celebrate!

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:56.450
Ryu-san's a cool guy, huh?

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:57.550
Right?

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.270
It isn't just his appearance...

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:01.780
It's like there's something inside him.

00:11:01.780 --> 00:11:04.090
Like he's standing really firm.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:07.270
<i>And you're amazing for understanding that.</i>

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:14.400
I was so nervous, feeling that 
immense spiritual pressure!

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:18.330
Fool? You get nervous?

00:11:18.330 --> 00:11:19.660
Yes.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:24.560
Even in the modern era, amazing mages 
still exist out there, don't they?

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:30.560
That's Ryu-san for you!

00:11:32.130 --> 00:11:35.880
Sorry that I'm not the one for you...

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:41.570
Ow!

00:11:58.020 --> 00:12:01.710
This place is always wonderful.

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:06.690
Ryu-san, is that a sword wound?

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:09.120
Yes, that's right.

00:12:09.530 --> 00:12:12.290
Yakuza are busy folks.

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:13.910
Yakuza?

00:12:14.460 --> 00:12:19.310
Sometimes, spiritualists help solve crimes.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:23.460
Ryu-san occasionally does.

00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:27.970
I think it was a desert in 
the American Midwest...

00:12:28.580 --> 00:12:32.810
There was a cult that sacrificed people.

00:12:33.550 --> 00:12:37.650
They burned them alive, and then 
the faithful would eat them!

00:12:38.810 --> 00:12:40.260
No, no...

00:12:40.260 --> 00:12:41.980
Broke them into bits and swallowed them.

00:12:41.980 --> 00:12:43.180
That isn't much better.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:51.040
Anyway, Ryu-san went in with 
the state police to stop them.

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.470
Wow!

00:12:52.470 --> 00:12:53.200
And?

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:55.670
A gunfight started.

00:12:57.550 --> 00:13:01.500
The original goal was to arrest the leaders

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.910
and break up the group, but...

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:06.740
Boom!

00:13:06.740 --> 00:13:10.480
In the end, the cultists 
blew up the building,

00:13:10.780 --> 00:13:12.350
and everyone died.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:15.170
That didn't go as I'd hoped...

00:13:15.600 --> 00:13:17.790
But I did save the hostages.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.800
<i>Is laughing at that okay?</i>

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:27.400
Well, they had planned a mass 
suicide to begin with.

00:13:27.750 --> 00:13:31.070
Some people just can't be saved.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:37.080
Ryu-san's a bit clumsy.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.670
So he always gets covered in wounds.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:42.340
What about you, Furuhonya-san?

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:47.710
Who was it that failed to recover a secret 
text from a group of Peruvian bandits,

00:13:47.710 --> 00:13:50.890
and was then shot with a machine gun?

00:13:51.090 --> 00:13:53.400
I only got hit twice!

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:57.800
Makes a painter's wounds from 
brawls feel like nothing, huh?

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.390
That's right.

00:13:59.390 --> 00:14:03.690
A scar from a yakuza's broken bottle 
isn't anything I can boast about.

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.360
No, no, no.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:09.530
And Reimei-san was almost killed 
by a fan who was stalking him.

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:12.640
She was a very passionate girl.

00:14:12.640 --> 00:14:15.210
Reimei-san, die with me!

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:18.360
Lucky it was a hardcover, huh?

00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:21.350
Sheesh, that's right!

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.140
Amazing...

00:14:28.700 --> 00:14:32.830
All those unbelievable experiences, 
and they're laughing about them.

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:36.380
Really, they are amazing.

00:14:37.150 --> 00:14:38.210
Hase?

00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:43.980
All the people who used to hang around me

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.290
were shallow suck-ups.

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:50.280
They were just old.

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:52.060
They weren't real adults.

00:14:53.350 --> 00:14:57.280
But everyone here is a real adult.

00:14:57.630 --> 00:14:58.790
Right?

00:14:59.140 --> 00:15:01.950
They're a little... no, very strange.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:06.270
But they all live their lives 
on their own terms.

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:08.170
They're real adults.

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:12.590
I think we kids really need

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:16.370
mentors and teachers like them.

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:20.440
Huh?

00:15:20.650 --> 00:15:22.730
What? An earthquake?

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:25.400
Are they working on the road?

00:15:25.910 --> 00:15:26.950
What's wrong?

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:36.560
What? A new guy?

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.820
Anyone from the apartment?

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.790
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:42.190
Oh, it's Matajuro!

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.660
Welcome back, chirp.

00:15:43.660 --> 00:15:46.490
Your face is as big as ever, chirp?

00:15:46.490 --> 00:15:49.210
But it's not only his face that's big, chirp!

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.460
Matajuro!

00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:52.430
M-Matajuro?

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:56.090
Hey, it's been a while, Matajuro-san.

00:15:56.540 --> 00:15:59.000
Oh, you are here!

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:04.530
I've brought delicious boar meat!

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:06.520
It's huge!

00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:08.610
Looks yummy.

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.700
There was a hunting match in Shirakami.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.520
And I won!

00:16:13.760 --> 00:16:15.380
Wow!

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:19.940
This is for the tengu in Kurama.

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:22.330
You get this.

00:16:22.330 --> 00:16:26.130
It's yummy 'cause it's on 
the verge of rotting!

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.700
So tengu are real. I guess that figures.

00:16:29.700 --> 00:16:31.790
Well, yokai are.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:35.290
How have you been, kid?

00:16:36.190 --> 00:16:40.570
Matajuro-san lives in a hidden village 
in the Kumano mountains.

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:41.890
A hidden village?

00:16:42.510 --> 00:16:46.570
Places with lots of mountains, 
like Kumano, Hida, and Shirakami,

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:48.620
have what are called "hidden villages."

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:52.760
They're just slightly out of phase with us,

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:54.990
or they have barriers,

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:57.030
so normal people can't enter.

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.450
But you know,

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:04.700
humans and those with different powers,

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:07.240
used to live in the same places.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:10.530
It's what you said before,

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:12.850
that mysteries are always with us.

00:17:13.380 --> 00:17:14.370
Indeed.

00:17:14.680 --> 00:17:17.590
But when the humans' numbers grew,

00:17:17.970 --> 00:17:23.430
they began to despise those who had 
different appearances and powers.

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.310
They drove them away,

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:27.450
and humans eventually forgot them.

00:17:34.290 --> 00:17:38.110
Why do we change like that?

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:40.900
Don't worry about it, kid.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:45.480
The people living in the 
mountains know the deal.

00:17:45.480 --> 00:17:49.200
They're surprised to see us, 
but they don't make a big fuss.

00:17:49.200 --> 00:17:52.370
Sometimes, they even give us smokes.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:53.290
See?

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.300
Thanks, Ruriko.

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:04.140
When I go into town, this is 
what I look forward to!

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.190
Delicious!

00:18:09.190 --> 00:18:13.070
Snacks are best when humans make them.

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:19.000
When I go to Kurama, I want to bring 
back lots of yummy Kyoto sweets!

00:18:19.300 --> 00:18:21.910
You like sweets, Matajuro-san?

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:26.950
Yes, when you give kids candy, 
they listen to what you say.

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:32.780
In our world, guys like him 
are disappearing, right?

00:18:32.780 --> 00:18:33.740
Yeah.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:41.830
We should be able to eat soon, huh?

00:18:42.270 --> 00:18:43.750
It looks good!

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:46.090
Ruriko-san made snacks!

00:18:46.090 --> 00:18:48.400
Fresh tuna sashimi!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:51.100
And fresh fried ginger, too!

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:53.770
Sashimi!

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.460
Thank you, Ruriko-san!

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:05.790
It's so good!

00:19:06.370 --> 00:19:10.450
Tuna's good with tea and 
rice and pickles, too.

00:19:10.800 --> 00:19:13.090
Okay, let's drink!

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:15.760
This is so much fun!

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:22.840
This looks really weird.

00:19:22.840 --> 00:19:26.830
But Matajuro-san, who lives alongside
 mysteries and nature,

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.210
and the people here

00:19:28.690 --> 00:19:31.600
are probably better off than we are, right?

00:19:34.310 --> 00:19:35.410
Ryu-san?

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:38.150
In the end, it's a problem of the heart.

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.000
People change.

00:19:40.330 --> 00:19:41.800
Believe in that,

00:19:41.800 --> 00:19:44.910
and begin by accepting your 
current way of life.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:46.970
Right!

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:54.310
<i>It's true that we can't return 
to the life we once had.</i>

00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:58.590
<i>But can we have a life that combines</i>

00:19:58.590 --> 00:20:01.760
<i>both of these worlds?</i>

00:20:04.090 --> 00:20:06.960
The world's a big place, huh?

00:20:07.210 --> 00:20:08.350
Right?

00:20:08.960 --> 00:20:11.010
When I come here, I really understand.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:15.890
I thought I was thinking about my future.

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:19.500
But I was only looking with a 
very short field of vision...

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:25.860
But it's okay to think more 
and be uncertain, right?

00:20:26.270 --> 00:20:27.310
Yeah.

00:20:28.130 --> 00:20:31.850
<i>We still have time.</i>

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:37.480
By the way, Inaba, is school going well?

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:39.340
Where's this coming from?

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:44.000
I thought you might have started being 
numb to things at the apartments.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:47.500
The Petit thing even scared me, after all.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.440
I know that.

00:20:49.440 --> 00:20:50.180
Also...

00:20:53.430 --> 00:20:56.810
Don't get involved in any weird stuff.

00:20:57.820 --> 00:20:58.870
Hase...

00:21:00.220 --> 00:21:04.770
"Weird"?! You don't mean me, do you?

00:21:04.770 --> 00:21:07.250
If so, I have no choice but to be upset...

00:21:07.250 --> 00:21:09.750
Hase-sama! Master!

00:21:13.920 --> 00:21:14.960
Kuri!

00:21:15.310 --> 00:21:16.840
Do something, Fool!

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:20.220
I'm not done talking yet, master!

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:31.170
I'm telling you... There are ghosts!

00:23:10.930 --> 00:23:13.620
There are scary stories everywhere, right?

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:15.930
The sound of a piano from an empty music room

00:23:15.930 --> 00:23:18.130
or you wake up at night, unable to move!

00:23:18.130 --> 00:23:20.170
Do you know any scary stories, Akine-san?

00:23:20.170 --> 00:23:24.680
Yes... A bowl of delicious 
rice suddenly vanishing!

00:23:25.490 --> 00:23:27.280
That always happens.

00:23:27.580 --> 00:23:30.540
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:30.220 --> 00:23:31.840
<b>Tenth Haunting 
School Ghost Stories?</b>

00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:31.840
School Ghost Stories?

00:23:31.840 --> 00:23:34.890
And when she stepped on the scale, 
a number she'd never seen...

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:35.920
Right, right.
